<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Fix Overflow</title>

    <style>
        * {
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 25px;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f3f4f6;
            color: #1f2937;
        }

        header {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
        }

        h1 {
            color: #2563eb;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 1000px;
            margin: auto;
        }

        .example {
            background-color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 25px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 3px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
        }

        h2 {
            color: #1e40af;
        }

        /* Example 1: Horizontal Overflow */
        .horizontal-box {
            width: 100%;
            overflow-x: auto;
            border: 2px solid #2563eb;
            padding: 12px;
        }

        .wide-content {
            width: 900px;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #dbeafe;
            white-space: nowrap;
        }

        /* Example 2: Text Overflow */
        .text-box {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 15px;
            background-color: #dcfce7;
            overflow-wrap: break-word;
            border: 1px solid #16a34a;
        }

        /* Example 3: Image Overflow */
        .image-box {
            width: 100%;
            border: 2px solid #f59e0b;
            padding: 10px;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .image-box img {
            max-width: 100%;
            height: auto;
            display: block;
        }

        /* Example 4: Fixed Height Overflow */
        .scroll-box {
            height: 120px;
            overflow-y: auto;
            padding: 15px;
            background-color: #fef3c7;
            border: 1px solid #d97706;
        }

        /* Example 5: Responsive Cards */
        .card-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 15px;
        }

        .card {
            flex: 1 1 200px;
            min-width: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            background-color: #ede9fe;
            border-radius: 8px;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 30px;
            color: #6b7280;
        }

        @media (max-width: 600px) {
            body {
                padding: 15px;
            }

            .example {
                padding: 15px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Fix Overflow in CSS</h1>
        <p>Learn how to prevent content from overflowing its container.</p>
    </header>

    <main class="container">

        <!-- Example 1 -->
        <section class="example">
            <h2>1. Horizontal Overflow</h2>
            <p>Scroll horizontally when content is wider than its container.</p>

            <div class="horizontal-box">
                <div class="wide-content">
                    This content is wider than the container. Scroll horizontally
                    to see the complete content.
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Example 2 -->
        <section class="example">
            <h2>2. Text Overflow</h2>
            <p>Long text should wrap instead of extending outside the box.</p>

            <div class="text-box">
                ThisIsAVeryLongWordWithoutSpacesThatCouldCauseHorizontalOverflow
                This text demonstrates how overflow-wrap: break-word fixes the issue.
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Example 3 -->
        <section class="example">
            <h2>3. Image Overflow</h2>
            <p>Use max-width: 100% to keep images inside their containers.</p>

            <div class="image-box">
                <img
                    src="https://placehold.co/1000x300/2563eb/ffffff?text=Responsive+Image"
                    alt="A blue responsive placeholder image"
                >
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Example 4 -->
        <section class="example">
            <h2>4. Vertical Overflow</h2>
            <p>Use overflow-y: auto to add vertical scrolling when needed.</p>

            <div class="scroll-box">
                <p>Line 1: This is sample content inside a fixed-height box.</p>
                <p>Line 2: The content continues below the visible area.</p>
                <p>Line 3: You can scroll vertically to read more.</p>
                <p>Line 4: CSS overflow-y controls vertical overflow.</p>
                <p>Line 5: This is the last line of the example.</p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Example 5 -->
        <section class="example">
            <h2>5. Responsive Cards</h2>
            <p>Flexbox with flex-wrap allows cards to move to the next row.</p>

            <div class="card-container">
                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Card One</h3>
                    <p>This card adjusts to the available screen width.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Card Two</h3>
                    <p>This card moves to another row on smaller screens.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="card">
                    <h3>Card Three</h3>
                    <p>Responsive layouts help prevent horizontal overflow.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>Fix Overflow Project | HTML and CSS Practice</p>
    </footer>

</body>
</html>